# Vexa — review ownership.
#
# The LAST matching rule wins, so the global fallback must stay at the top:
# every rule below it overrides it. Moving `*` to the bottom would make the
# Team Lead the only reviewer for the whole repository.
#
# GitHub excludes the PR author from its own reviewer list. That is why every
# path has at least two owners — otherwise an owner's PR gets no reviewer and
# hangs forever. The only exception is /.github/, see the note at the bottom.

# Global fallback — Team Lead reviews everything by default
*                       @terekh373

# Backend: Team Lead + backend dev
/apps/api/              @terekh373 @suberbobbr

# Database contract: schema, migrations, seed.
/apps/api/prisma/       @terekh373 @suberbobbr
/docs/schema.dbml       @terekh373 @suberbobbr

# Shared contract between backend and clients
/packages/shared/       @terekh373 @suberbobbr

# Frontend web + mobile. Four owners for the catch-up sprint: both frontend
# devs are unavailable, and the Team Lead plus the backend dev are taking
# their tasks. Any single approval satisfies the rule.
/apps/web/              @terekh373 @suberbobbr @devitfro @voer2
/apps/mobile/           @terekh373 @suberbobbr @devitfro @voer2

# Workflow configuration and this file itself. Two owners so a change here
# can never deadlock: GitHub excludes the PR author from its own reviewers.
/.github/               @terekh373 @suberbobbr